(CARCASSONNE - Demo Rulebook \(Board Game Cafe\)) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(OVERVIEW) Tj T*
(Players build a medieval landscape tile by tile and place followers \(meeples\) on) Tj T*
(roads, cities, monasteries and fields to score points.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(SETUP) Tj T*
(Put the start tile in the middle and shuffle the remaining 71 tiles face down. Each) Tj T*
(player takes 8 followers of one color and puts one on the score track, keeping 7 in) Tj T*
(supply.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(YOUR TURN) Tj T*
(1. Draw a tile and place it touching at least one tile already in play. All touching) Tj T*
(   edges must) Tj T*
(   match: roads to roads, cities to cities, fields to fields. If a tile cannot be) Tj T*
(   placed anywhere,) Tj T*
(   discard it and draw another.) Tj T*
(2. You may place one follower from your supply on the tile you just placed: on a road) Tj T*
(   \(thief\),) Tj T*
(   in a city \(knight\), on a monastery \(monk\) or on a field \(farmer\). You may not place) Tj T*
(   a follower) Tj T*
(   on a feature that already has a follower, even far away.) Tj T*
(3. Score every feature completed by your tile. Followers on scored features go back to) Tj T*
(   their) Tj T*
(   owners.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
